From: DoM!niC <info@dom1nic.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: x1e80100-microsoft-romulus: add DisplayPort
 audio links

The sound node of the Surface Laptop 7 has DAI links for the speakers, the
headset codec and the microphones only. The DP controllers mdss_dp0 and
mdss_dp1 (the two USB-C ports) are enabled and carry #sound-dai-cells, the
audio topology (X1E80100-Romulus-tplg.bin) routes MultiMedia1 to
DISPLAY_PORT_RX_0/1 and the machine driver creates the "DP0 Jack"/"DP1 Jack"
controls the ALSA UCM profile expects, but without backend links the card
has no path to the controllers and a monitor's audio output stays silent.

Add the two links in the form the other X1E80100 boards use
(x1e80100-crd.dts, x1e78100-lenovo-thinkpad-t14s.dtsi). mdss_dp2 is not
wired on this device and stays disabled.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi
@@ -381,6 +381,38 @@
 				"VA DMIC1", "VA MIC BIAS3",
 				"TX SWR_INPUT1", "ADC2_OUTPUT";
 
+		dp0-dai-link {
+			link-name = "DP0 Playback";
+
+			cpu {
+				sound-dai = <&q6apmbedai DISPLAY_PORT_RX_0>;
+			};
+
+			codec {
+				sound-dai = <&mdss_dp0>;
+			};
+
+			platform {
+				sound-dai = <&q6apm>;
+			};
+		};
+
+		dp1-dai-link {
+			link-name = "DP1 Playback";
+
+			cpu {
+				sound-dai = <&q6apmbedai DISPLAY_PORT_RX_1>;
+			};
+
+			codec {
+				sound-dai = <&mdss_dp1>;
+			};
+
+			platform {
+				sound-dai = <&q6apm>;
+			};
+		};
+
 		va-dai-link {
 			link-name = "VA Capture";
 
